<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3092" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκερσεκόμης</span></b>  (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκερσι-</span> in <i><span class="en">
			Nonn.
		</span></i>
		<i><span class="en">
			Il.
		</span></i> cc. infr.), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, (
			Dor.
		 voc. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κόμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>Pae.</u>
					9.45
				</span></i>
			: dat. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κόμοισιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nonn.
					<u>D.</u>
					14.232
				</span></i>
			), (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κείρω, κόμη</span>) <i>with unshorn
				hair</i>, i.e. <i>ever-young</i> (for Greek youths wore long
			hair till they reached manhood), of Phoebus, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				20.39
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Ap.</u>
				134
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>long-haired</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				10.29
			</span></i>, al.; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκειρεκόμης</span>.</div>
